---
import MotionPage from '@/components/MotionPage.astro';
import MotionStage from '@/components/motion/MotionStage.astro';
import MotionUsage from '@/components/motion/MotionUsage.astro';
import MotionOptions from '@/components/motion/MotionOptions.astro';
import MotionTokens from '@/components/motion/MotionTokens.astro';
import Loop from '@/components/motion/scenes/Loop.astro';
import LoopControls from '@/components/motion/scenes/LoopControls.astro';
import { MotionLoopReact } from '@/examples/react/motion-loop.tsx';
import { MotionLoopAngular } from '@/examples/angular/motion-loop.ts';
import MotionLoopSvelte from '@/examples/svelte/motion-loop.svelte';
---
<MotionPage
  slug="loop"
  title="Motion: loop, and pause it"
  description="A loop plays forever, rests when it is off-screen, and always comes with a way to pause it. In HTML, React, Angular and Svelte."
>
  <MotionStage scene="loop" label="Live example: Loop, and pause it" height="sm">
    <Fragment slot="controls"><LoopControls /></Fragment>
    <Loop size="page" />
  </MotionStage>

  <h2>How to use it</h2>
  <p>
    A loop plays its keyframes forever, from the moment it is bound. It pauses by itself while its element is out of view, and
    plays again when the element comes back. The presets <code>rotate</code> (a full turn each second), <code>breathe</code>
    (swells to 104 % and back) and <code>blink</code> (one dim flash each second) are loops.
  </p>
  <pre><code>{`<span data-motion="rotate" class="spinner"></span>

import { defineMotion } from '@udixio/motion';

defineMotion('spin', {
  verb: 'loop',
  keyframes: [{ rotate: 0 }, { rotate: 360 }],
  pause: 'control',
});`}</code></pre>
  <p>
    WCAG 2.2.2 asks that moving, blinking or scrolling content which starts by itself, lasts more than five seconds and runs
    beside other content can be paused, stopped or hidden, unless it is essential. A loop therefore states in its definition
    how it is paused:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><code>pause: 'control'</code>: the page offers a visible control that pauses the loop. The presets use it.</li>
    <li><code>pause: 'essential'</code> with a <code>reason</code>: the loop is the content itself, such as an indeterminate progress indicator. The validator requires the reason, and refuses it on a <code>control</code> loop.</li>
  </ul>
  <pre><code>{`defineMotion('indeterminate', {
  verb: 'loop',
  keyframes: [{ x: -140 }, { x: 340 }],
  pause: 'essential',
  reason: 'The bar shows that work is running; a paused bar would look finished.',
});`}</code></pre>

  <h2>Pause from the page</h2>
  <p>
    The page pauses a loop with the attribute <code>data-motion-paused</code>, or from script with the binding's
    <code>pause()</code>, and plays it again by removing the attribute or with <code>play()</code>, which clears the pause.
  </p>
  <pre><code>{`spinner.setAttribute('data-motion-paused', '');
spinner.removeAttribute('data-motion-paused');

getMotion(spinner, 'loop')?.pause();
getMotion(spinner, 'loop')?.play(); // clears the pause`}</code></pre>

  <h2>Use it in the frameworks</h2>
  <p>
    The loop takes a <code>paused</code> option: React <code>useMotion('rotate', &#123; paused &#125;)</code>, Angular
    <code>[udxMotionPaused]</code>, Svelte <code>&#123;&#64;attach motion('rotate', () =&gt; (&#123; paused &#125;))&#125;</code>.
  </p>
  <MotionUsage name="motion-loop">
    <MotionLoopReact slot="react" client:visible />
    <MotionLoopAngular slot="angular" client:visible />
    <MotionLoopSvelte slot="svelte" client:visible />
  </MotionUsage>

  <h2>Options</h2>
  <MotionOptions verb="loop" />

  <h2>Timing and tokens</h2>
  <p>A loop has no spring: its <code>timing</code> is a curve only, <code>&#123; duration, easing &#125;</code>. Without <code>timing</code> it runs for one second, linearly.</p>
  <MotionTokens tokens={['duration.extraLong4', 'easing.linear']} />

  <h2>Reduced motion</h2>
  <p>
    Under reduced motion, or with <code>--udx-motion: none</code>, a loop does not play: the element keeps its stylesheet
    state. The pause control still works for the loops that play. See <a href="/motion/accessibility">Reduced motion</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Limits</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A loop with <code>pause: 'control'</code> needs a visible control on the page to be pausable.</li>
    <li><code>--udx-motion-scale</code> scales its duration and the distances of its keyframes, and 0 stops it.</li>
  </ul>
</MotionPage>
